    { "type": "paragraph", "html": "Without these animals, forest closed in far beyond its natural range. The dense oak–lime–alder canopy of the Atlantic period — long treated as Europe's \"natural\" baseline — was in fact an ecological anomaly: the densest Europe had been in over twenty million years, and a direct consequence of defaunation rather than climate alone." },
